the deep blues of water anamorphic  lenses and contemplative MCU story  wakanda forever passionately honors the  legacy of Chadwick Boseman it's no  secret that black panther wakanda  forever is one of the most highly  anticipated MCU films so far the movie  serves both as a sequel to The Beloved  2018 Blockbuster Black Panther and as a  climactic finale to Marvel's phase 4 and  yet overshadowing all of the excitement  for wakanda forever is the notable  absence of actor Chadwick Boseman who  tragically passed away in 2020 following  an extended battle with colon cancer  from what we've seen thus far in the  trailers for wakanda forever it's clear  that Bozeman's Legacy will be a major  component of the film itself indeed it  appears that much of the film story will  be informed by the devastating loss of  Chadwick Boseman director Ryan coogler  confirmed earlier this year when he said  that the cast and crew put their love  for Chadwick into the film while  presenting a preview for the movie at  San Diego Comic-Con in fact Bozeman's  impact on wakanda forever is so great  that even the film's visual style was  influenced by his passing in a recent  interview with Entertainment Weekly  coogler mentioned how the visual style  of the movie is supposed to reflect the  immense loss felt after Bozeman's stats  he said I think this film has the fog of  loss over it anamorphic lenses warped  the image a little bit sometimes when  you go through profound loss it can warp  how you look at the world what we were  after was just making it feel tactile  even though it felt like a dream coogler  went on to explain that this is meant to  craft a film that is both intimate and  emotionally poignant while operating on  the scale of a massive superhero  Blockbuster in addition to the use of  warped lenses coogler addressed how the  shift in visual style includes an  emphasis on water and the color blue  something that should come as no  surprise since the film's primary  antagonist name or the Submariner is the  ruler of a vast undersea Kingdom what  contact will form of course since lost  and grief have so heavily informed the  storytelling and style of wakanda  forever it's no surprised that the  experience making it was melancholic for  those who knew and worked with Bozeman  on the previous movie while speaking to  collider Winston Duke who plays mbaku  explained that shooting the sequel was  strange without their old colleague on  the set however the experience helped  them come to terms with his death and  understand the grieving process Duke  said it was something that we dealt with  every day and something that we got to  understand every day that we're not the  only people grieving not only the people  who are in front of the camera are  grieving it's everybody elsewhere Lupita  Nyong'o who portrays Nakia recalled  having to meditate pray and reflect in  order to come to grips with the new  movie existing without her friend and  co-star it took the actress a while to  adjust to the idea of a sequel without  Bozeman but she understood that changes  were necessary she told the New York  Times I found myself having to radically  accept that this was going to be  different and that showing up with as  much openness as possible was key  wakanda forever was certainly an  emotional experience for everyone  involved but the movie promises to honor  the Legacy of both Bozeman and King  t'challa  [Music]
 

